this sort of came up last week and I got  an audience question about it that's  interesting and the question is hey  David a lot of liberals oppose nuclear  technology aren't liberals wrong to  oppose nuclear technology I've actually  talked about this before and whenever I  say this I end up angering almost  everybody on the one hand it's  absolutely true that we should not be  looking to nuclear energy as the panacea  for the long term of humanity we should  be looking at alternative and renewable  sources of energy we know that humanity  is able to harness those renewable and  alternative sources of energy in a way  that they can provide for all of our  energy needs  don't fall for the right wing talking  point that alternative and renewable  energy can never provide the energy that  we need  I think we're liberals sometimes go  wrong is it's true that there are risks  to nuclear energy but new nuclear that  would be put in place now has so  significantly dealt with a lot of those  risks that the sort of expected value  the expected likelihood of a major  disaster is very very low and there's a  lot of people on the Left who don't like  to hear that so what I've said before  and what I will repeat is that I am not  opposed to nuclear tech nuclear energy  as a bridge to getting off of some of  these dirtier fossil fuels like coal and  others while we ramp up truly  alternative and renewable sources of  energy and I think that the left should  be more open to that you do run into a  practical question though which is that  to significantly increase nuclear  capacity takes a while and there's a  question and there is disagreement about  this there's really good studies that  argue both sides of this there's the  question of by the time you get  significant new nuclear capacity up and  running shouldn't we or couldn't we  already be heavily transitioned off of  fossil fuels and over to alternatives  and renewables anyway and I and  that is where I am sort of less certain  but I do believe that there is a  reflexive anti-nuclear stands that many  on the Left take which I would like to  see sort of replaced with a more  pragmatic nuclear energy technology has  changed significantly over the last 40  years it is significantly safer and  while we shouldn't be for it  for the long term being open to  increases in nuclear energy capacity as  a bridge to getting off of fossil fuels  is something I wish that progressives  would be more willing to consider send  me your thoughts we've got a great bonus  show for you today the show doesn't have  to end now if you are a member or a  patron you can get instant access to the  bonus show another 15 to 20 minutes  every day just for our paid subscribers  hope to speak to you then
 

